 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Yes—today (Saturday, October 17), it would be prudent to stay indoors as much as you can.** Kuala Lumpur’s latest reported Department of Environment reading is **API 161 (“Unhealthy”)**; readings can vary by neighborhood. With asthma, avoid outdoor exercise and other strenuous activity outside today. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuala-lumpur))\n\nKeep windows closed, run air conditioning with the fresh-air intake closed if available, and follow your asthma action plan. Keep your reliever inhaler with you. If you must go out, keep it brief; a well-fitting N95 can reduce exposure to particles. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/air-quality-and-health/fires-and-your-health/?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf your symptoms worsen or your reliever isn’t helping, seek medical care; get emergency help for severe trouble breathing. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/air-quality-and-health/fires-and-your-health/?utm_source=openai))",
